nder, {time 15-18 min}. Drain, return to the pot and mash with the butter, warm milk and salt until smooth.","uses":[0,1,2,3]},{"text":"Meanwhile heat the oven to {temp 400F oven}. Heat the oil in the skillet over medium-high heat and brown the beef, breaking it up, {time 6-8 min}. Spoon off excess fat.","uses":[5,6]},{"text":"Add the onion and carrots and cook until softened, {time 6 min}. Stir in the garlic, flour and tomato paste for {time 1 min}.","uses":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"text":"Stir in the broth, Worcestershire, thyme and salt and simmer until thick and gravy-like, {time 8-10 min}. Stir in the peas and spread the filling in the baking dish.","uses":[12,13,14,15,16]},{"text":"Spoon the mash over the top, spread it to the edges and rough up the surface with a fork. Sprinkle with cheese, if using.","uses":[4]},{"text":"Bake until the filling bubbles at the edges and the top is golden, {time 20-25 min}. Rest for {time 10 min} before serving.","uses":[]}]}